# A pass written in Python, run as py:<path>. It sees what the C++ passes
# already concluded (labels, names) and writes back into the same annotation
# table, so its comments interleave with theirs in one listing.
#
# The blob is:  sub sp,#0x20 / str x0,[sp,#8] / ldr x1,[sp,#8] / mul x3,x1,x1 /
#               add sp,#0x20 / ret
#
# RUN: %sleigh-poc --sla=%specs/AARCH64.sla --base=0 \
# RUN:   --bytes=ff8300d1e00700f9e10740f9237c019bff830091c0035fd6 \
# RUN:   --passes=stack-vars,rename,py:%S/annotate.py,print-ssa | FileCheck %s

# CHECK: applied 3 directive(s)

# The block comment the script emitted, next to the one stack-vars emitted.
# CHECK: block 0 (entry)
# CHECK-DAG: ; frame: var_18[8]
# CHECK-DAG: ; seen by python on AARCH64

# The script labelled the multiply's result, and print-ssa renders it exactly
# like a label set from C++ -- version suffix and all.
# CHECK: product#0 = INT_MULT
# CHECK-SAME: ; multiply, worth a look


# A script that fails is reported, not fatal: the rest of the pipeline still
# runs.
# RUN: %sleigh-poc --sla=%specs/AARCH64.sla --base=0 --bytes=c0035fd6 \
# RUN:   --passes=py:/nonexistent/script.py,print-ssa | FileCheck --check-prefix=MISSING %s

# MISSING: /nonexistent/script.py: script exited with status
# MISSING: RETURN
